%%{init: {"flowchart": {"wrappingWidth": 320}}}%%
%% ADMM (proximal message passing): every device steps near its last plan; a shared price moves with the imbalance.
flowchart TB
  S(["<b>Start</b><br/>every plan zero but the household load's; price zero (or a warm start)"]) --> A
  subgraph R["One iteration, repeated"]
    direction TB
    A["<b>Every terminal, at the same time</b><br/>its cheapest plan near a target: its last plan, moved by the imbalance and the price<br/>devices: their proximal step, by any solver (a DP; an LP for a battery), no tariff; the tank and HVAC relaxed<br/>grid connection: the bill and the limits, in closed form"]
    B["<b>The house</b><br/>average the imbalance; raise the price where it persists<br/>make the plan runnable (tank, HVAC on/off) and keep the best so far"]
    A -- "plans" --> B
    B -- "imbalance, price" --> A
  end
  B -- "the plans settle, or 100 iterations" --> E(["<b>Result</b><br/>the best runnable plan, then a polish: devices re-plan one at a time, kept only if cheaper<br/><i>no bound: how far from the best is unknown</i>"])
